// Adversarial: Conductor swaps PrimaryBolt <-> ExtraBolt markers between the bumped extra
// and the current primary on every Perfect BumpPerformed. Prism breaker spawns ExtraBolt
// entities on Perfect bumps, providing a live population of extras for Conductor to swap.
// The adversarial risk: rapid Perfect bumps can fire Conductor multiple times in quick
// succession — at-most-one-swap-per-tick logic must hold or stale pre-flush PrimaryBolt
// observations produce duplicate markers. Chaos input at 0.7 drives frequent bumps including
// Perfect grades, exercising the swap path under pressure. The ExactlyOnePrimaryBolt invariant
// enforces the core Conductor invariant: exactly one PrimaryBolt must exist at all times
// while bolts are present. BoltInBounds catches any bolt that escapes due to a corrupted
// effect tree after a swap. NoNaN detects velocity corruption from a stale effect walk
// on the wrong bolt post-swap. BoltSpeedAccurate detects speed drift from effect-tree
// duplication if BoundEffects are incorrectly cloned rather than moved. NoEntityLeaks
// verifies that swap-spawned ExtraBolt entities (via Prism) are properly cleaned up.
// ValidDashState guards against breaker state machine corruption under the chaos pattern.
// Scatter layout maximises the variety of bump geometries and Perfect-bump rates.
// Stress: 32 parallel copies explore seed-varied paths through the swap trigger distribution.
(
    breaker: "Prism",
    layout: "Scatter",
    input: Chaos((action_prob: 0.7)),
    max_frames: 2000,
    disallowed_failures: [ExactlyOnePrimaryBolt, NoNaN, BoltInBounds, BoltSpeedAccurate, ValidDashState, BreakerInBounds, BreakerCountReasonable, NoEntityLeaks, BoltCountReasonable],
    allowed_failures: None,
    debug_setup: None,
    invariant_params: (max_bolt_count: 16),
    allow_early_end: false,
    stress: (runs: 32, parallelism: 32),
    seed: 42,
    frame_mutations: [
        (frame: 10, mutation: InjectProtocol(kind_name: "Conductor")),
    ],
)
